[
  {
    "id": "P0001",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The existing test suites pass, but ordinary regression probes found incorrect parsing, rendering, source ranges, CLI behavior, and one feature-specific build failure. Findings: **1 High, 12 Medium, 3 Low**. Behavioral findings below were reproduced locally; the SIMD-contract finding is from source inspection.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0002",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "High\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0003",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Enabling `getopts` without `html` breaks the binary build\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0004",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`pulldown-cmark/src/main.rs:25`; supporting configuration: `pulldown-cmark/Cargo.toml:27`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0005",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: an enabled binary has its required dependencies. Observed: `cargo check --locked -p pulldown-cmark --no-default-features --features getopts` fails with unresolved import `pulldown_cmark::html`. The binary requires only `getopts`, although it unconditionally imports the feature-gated renderer.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0006",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Consequence: this selectable package configuration cannot build. Require both features for the binary, or make the CLI feature enable HTML. Add this configuration to build checks.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0007",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Medium\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0008",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "CLI input and output failures are mishandled\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0009",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Locations: `pulldown-cmark/src/main.rs:172`, `:184`, `:219`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0010",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: unsuccessful reads or writes produce a diagnostic and unsuccessful exit status. Executed probes found:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0011",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "- Invalid UTF-8 stdin: empty output, exit **0**.\n- Output redirected to `/dev/full`: exit **0**.\n- Missing input file: panic, exit **101**.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0012",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Consequence: pipelines can report success despite producing no usable output. Propagate I/O errors consistently, return a result from the rendering helper, and explicitly flush its `BufWriter`; drop-time flush errors otherwise remain invisible.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0013",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Processing multiple files repeats earlier content\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0014",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`pulldown-cmark/src/main.rs:167`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0015",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: each file contributes its contents once. Observed: files containing `Alpha\\n` and `Beta\\n` produce:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0016",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "```html\n<p>Alpha</p>\n<p>Alpha\nBeta</p>\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0017",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`read_to_string` appends to the reused buffer, which is rendered after every file.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0018",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Consequence: batch conversion duplicates content and can merge unrelated Markdown structures. Clear the buffer per file, or concatenate all inputs and render once. Add a two-file CLI regression.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0019",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "CRLF becomes two spaces inside code spans\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0020",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`pulldown-cmark/src/parse.rs:1340`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0021",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: CommonMark treats CRLF as one line ending, converted to one space inside a code span. Observed: input `` `a\\r\\nb` `` produces `<code>a  b</code>`; LF and standalone CR produce one space. The same problem occurs inside blockquotes.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0022",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Consequence: Windows-authored Markdown changes code text. Consume the complete line ending using `scan_eol`, then append one space. Extend the existing newline-in-code tests with CRLF.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0023",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "A trailing tab prevents a code fence from closing\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0024",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`pulldown-cmark/src/scanners.rs:528`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0025",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: CommonMark permits spaces or tabs after a closing fence. Observed: `\"```\\ncode\\n```\\t\\nafter\\n\"` renders the closing fence and `after` inside the code block.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0026",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Consequence: an ordinary trailing tab changes the remainder of the document\u2019s structure. Scan both spaces and tabs before checking the line ending; test both fence characters.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0027",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Case-insensitive footnote matches produce broken HTML links\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0028",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Locations: `pulldown-cmark/src/html.rs:53`, `:139`; related reference emission: `pulldown-cmark/src/parse.rs:768`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0029",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: references accepted as matching the same definition share its destination and number. Observed:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0030",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "```markdown\nref [^FOO] [^foo]\n\n[^foo]: Note\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0031",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "produces references to `#FOO` numbered 1 and `#foo` numbered 2, while only `id=\"foo\"` exists. Unicode case-folding variants also receive separate numbers and unmatched destinations.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0032",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Consequence: accepted footnote references fail to navigate and display inconsistent numbering. Resolve references to a canonical definition identifier and use the same case-folded identity for numbering. Add ASCII and Unicode case-variant tests.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0033",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "HTML I/O rendering silently truncates output on successful short writes. pulldown-cmark/src/html.rs:595. Passing a conforming std::io::Write implementation that accepts only two bytes per write to html::write_html_io loses the unwritten suffixes of tags and text. The streaming rendering path treats each successful write as completion of the whole fragment instead of retrying the remaining bytes. Rendering an ordered list such as \"3. caf\u00e9 & tea\" can therefore return Ok while producing incomplete HTML.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0034",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Standalone CR line endings are inconsistently recognized\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0035",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`pulldown-cmark/src/scanners.rs:508`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0036",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: CommonMark accepts LF, CRLF, and standalone CR. Observed: `scan_nextline` searches only for LF. With heading attributes enabled, `\"# heading\\r\\rpara\\r\"` becomes one heading containing the following paragraph. Executed probes also found incorrect fenced-code, indented-code, and HTML-block behavior with CR-only input.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0037",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Consequence: valid documents can acquire substantially different block structure. Make line scanning recognize all documented endings and verify affected block consumers with equivalent fixtures.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0038",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Link-label length counts non-ASCII bytes and ignores ordinary ASCII\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0039",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`pulldown-cmark/src/linklabel.rs:122`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0040",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: labels contain at most 999 Unicode characters. Observed boundary probes:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0041",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "- 499 `\u00e9` characters resolve; 500 do not.\n- 249 crab emoji resolve; 250 do not.\n- 1,000 ASCII `a` characters still resolve.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0042",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The counter increments for every non-ASCII byte and does not increment for ordinary ASCII letters.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0043",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Consequence: valid internationalized reference labels are rejected, while over-limit ASCII labels are accepted. Count Unicode characters consistently, including escaped and whitespace portions. Add boundary tests for several UTF-8 widths.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0044",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Wikilink source ranges omit the final bracket\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0045",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`pulldown-cmark/src/parse.rs:944`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0046",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: `OffsetIter` returns the corresponding complete source range. Observed: `[[Wiki]]` produces link start/end ranges `0..7`, although the construct occupies `0..8`. Embedded wikilink images have the same off-by-one error.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0047",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Consequence: editors and source transformations leave a bracket behind or select incomplete syntax. Use the end of the second closing delimiter and assert complete ranges for links and images.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0048",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Empty wikilink aliases render delimiter text\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0049",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`pulldown-cmark/src/parse.rs:900`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0050",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: closing delimiters remain syntax when handling an empty display label. Observed: `[[Wiki|]]` renders:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0051",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "```html\n<p><a href=\"Wiki\">]]</a></p>\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0052",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The selected child starts at a closing-bracket node.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0053",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Consequence: boundary-case input generates visibly incorrect link text. Handle an empty alias explicitly\u2014either according to a documented empty-label behavior or as literal Markdown\u2014and keep delimiter nodes outside its children.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0054",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Single-character heading attributes are silently dropped\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0055",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`pulldown-cmark/src/firstpass.rs:2548`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0056",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: documented custom attributes without values are retained regardless of name length. Observed: with heading attributes enabled, `# heading {x}` renders `<h1>heading</h1>`, losing `x`; longer attribute names work.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0057",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Consequence: callers lose attributes from both parsed events and rendered HTML. Apply the length restriction only to prefixed ID/class forms, and test one-character custom attributes.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0058",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Literal NUL is retained instead of replaced\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0059",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`pulldown-cmark/src/firstpass.rs:2355`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0060",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: the bundled CommonMark contract requires U+0000 to become U+FFFD. Observed: ordinary input `\"a\\0b\"` renders `\"<p>a\\0b</p>\\n\"`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0061",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Consequence: output text contradicts the claimed CommonMark normalization. Normalize literal NUL while preserving source offsets, and add event and renderer regressions. This was checked solely as a correctness case; no security impact was investigated.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0062",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "SIMD unchecked-access contracts are incomplete\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0063",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Locations: `pulldown-cmark/src/firstpass.rs:2644`, `:2693`, `:2703`, `:2733`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0064",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Source inspection found three unsafe functions without complete safety contracts and one explicit unsafe block without a SAFETY justification. In particular, `process_mask` does not document the relationship required between mask bits, offset, and `bytes.get_unchecked`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0065",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Consequence: future scanner changes lack a written basis for preserving unchecked-access preconditions. Document the bounds, mask, and CPU-feature obligations and justify each unsafe call. No invalid access was demonstrated; this x86_64 implementation was not executed on the aarch64 host.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0066",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Low\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0067",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Tab-separated fence metadata becomes extra CSS classes\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0068",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`pulldown-cmark/src/html.rs:261`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0069",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: the renderer\u2019s established first-word behavior treats a tab like a space. Observed: a fence info string `rust\\tcustom` produces `class=\"language-rust\\tcustom\"`; `rust custom` produces only `class=\"language-rust\"`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0070",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Consequence: metadata unexpectedly becomes additional class tokens. Split on the intended whitespace class and extend the existing info-string tests. This concerns renderer consistency; CommonMark leaves info-string rendering discretionary.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0071",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Public documentation has omissions and an incorrect punctuation example\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0072",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Locations: `pulldown-cmark/src/parse.rs:181`, `pulldown-cmark/src/html.rs:590`, `:625`, `pulldown-cmark/src/lib.rs:674`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0073",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The advisory pass reported **65 library missing-documentation warning sites** and two missing `# Errors` sections. The consequential omissions include offset units on `BrokenLink::span` and writer-error behavior.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0074",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Separately, smart-punctuation documentation promises that `--` becomes an em dash. Executed input `a -- ---` produces an en dash followed by an em dash, consistent with the existing implementation\u2019s convention.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0075",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Clarify the API contracts and correct the example.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0076",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Strict Clippy fails on the supplied toolchain\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0077",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Example locations: `pulldown-cmark/src/lib.rs:636`, `pulldown-cmark/src/utils.rs:5`, `pulldown-cmark/src/parse.rs:468`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0078",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: the requested strict lint gate completes. Observed on Rust **1.99.1**:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0079",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "- All features: four build-script diagnostics stop compilation.\n- `serde,simd` without `gen-tests`: 23 library diagnostics, including documentation-list formatting, unnecessary borrows, and simplifiable expressions.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0080",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Consequence: strict lint checks cannot currently pass. These are pre-existing baseline failures under the review configuration. Older toolchains were not run, so toolchain drift alone is not established.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0081",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Verification and evidence\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0082",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Commands ran offline with `RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0`, from `/work/crate` unless specified.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0083",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "| Command | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo test --locked -p pulldown-cmark` | Passed: 1,255 tests including doctests |\n| `cargo test --locked -p pulldown-cmark --all-features` | Passed: 1,260 |\n| `cargo test --locked -p pulldown-cmark --no-default-features` | Passed: 79 |\n| `cargo fmt --all --check` | Passed |\n| `cargo clippy --locked -p pulldown-cmark --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings` | Failed: four build-script diagnostics |\n| `cargo clippy --locked -p pulldown-cmark --all-targets --features serde,simd -- -D warnings` | Failed: 23 library diagnostics |\n| `RUSTDOCFLAGS=\"-D warnings\" cargo doc --locked -p pulldown-cmark --no-deps --document-private-items --all-features` | Passed |\n| `cargo check --locked -p pulldown-cmark --no-default-features --features getopts` | Failed: unresolved `html` import |\n| `cargo +nightly-2026-10-01 miri test --locked -p pulldown-cmark --lib` | Passed: 59 unit tests |\n| `cargo test --offline --manifest-path /work/tmp/review-harness/Cargo.toml` | Intentional regression failures: 11 failed, one passed |\n| `python3 /work/tmp/cli-regressions.py` | Four expected-behavior checks failed |\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0084",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The required `bash /work/[tooling]/scripts/[tooling] --audit /work/crate` passed formatting, but workspace rustdoc/tests were blocked by supporting `mozjs_sys` tooling: `llvm-objdump` was unavailable. Workspace Clippy also encountered the build-script failures above. These supporting-package/tool failures do not establish parser defects.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0085",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The advisory lint pass and heuristic scan completed. Style-only scan suggestions without a concrete consequence were excluded. Scratch Rust formatting, Clippy, and documentation checks passed. Reproductions and logs remain under `/work/tmp`, including [regression tests](/work/tmp/review-harness/tests/regressions.rs), [CLI probes](/work/tmp/cli-regressions.py), and [gate output](/work/tmp/gate.log).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0086",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Review-authored changes were confined to scratch files. All-features commands enabled `gen-tests`, which regenerated files under `pulldown-cmark/tests/suite`; production source was not edited.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0087",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Final count: findings\u20141 High, 12 Medium, 3 Low. Coverage was focused rather than exhaustive. No dedicated security, fuzzing, or performance assessment was performed. MSRV, cross-target builds, and x86 SIMD execution were unrun; those toolchains/targets were unavailable. Feature-powerset tooling was unavailable. Last `/work/clock` reading: **509.1 seconds of 2,700**, at **2026-11-03 19:58:20 UTC**."
  },
  {
    "id": "P0088",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Found **14 correctness/build issues**. The existing test suites pass, but added local regressions reproduce the failures below. All behavioral findings are supported by executed tests and source inspection.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0089",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "HTML blocks ignore valid closing tags. [firstpass.rs:1250](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/firstpass.rs:1250) uses a case-sensitive search for the opening tag\u2019s corresponding closing tag. CommonMark permits case-insensitive closing tags and, for these blocks, does not require matching tag names. Both `<script>\\nx\\n</SCRIPT>\\n\\nafter` and `<pre>\\nx\\n</style>\\n\\nafter` incorrectly absorb `after` into the HTML block instead of emitting `<p>after</p>`. Ordinary documents can lose Markdown rendering for their remaining content.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0090",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Table rows with missing trailing cells emit too few cells. pulldown-cmark/src/firstpass.rs:519. parse_table_row_inner returns a short body row after scanning only the cells physically present on its line, without adding the missing trailing cells required by the table header. With ENABLE_TABLES, a three-column table followed by the body row | one | emits one TableCell and renders only one td rather than three. Consumers that depend on a consistent column count receive ragged event rows and HTML.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0091",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "A trailing tab prevents a code fence from closing. [scanners.rs:528](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/scanners.rs:528) accepts only spaces after closing backticks. CommonMark permits spaces or tabs. For `\"```\\nx\\n```\\t\\nafter\"`, the closing fence and `after` become code content. A trailing editor-inserted tab can therefore change the rest of a document\u2019s structure.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0092",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "The CLI renders previous files again when given multiple files. [main.rs:173](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/main.rs:173) appends every file to the same `String`, then renders that accumulated string on every iteration. Files containing `\"one\\n\"` and `\"two\\n\"` produce:\n   ```html\n   <p>one</p>\n   <p>one\n   two</p>\n   ```\n   Expected behavior is to render each input once. Batch callers receive duplicated content and potentially changed Markdown structure.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0093",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "The CLI silently discards I/O failures. [main.rs:184](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/main.rs:184) ignores stdin read errors; [main.rs:219](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/main.rs:219) ignores rendering/write errors. Tests supplying invalid UTF-8 through stdin and closing the stdout pipe both observed exit status **0**, with no diagnostic. Callers cannot distinguish successful conversion from missing output.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0094",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Case-insensitive footnote references produce inconsistent anchors and numbers. [html.rs:141](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/html.rs:141) and [html.rs:382](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/html.rs:382) use the original, case-sensitive label strings, although parser lookup folds case. With `a[^NOTE] b[^note]\\n\\n[^Note]: text\\n`, the references target `#NOTE` and `#note`, numbered 1 and 2; the definition has ID `Note`, numbered 3. Recognized references should share a number and resolve to their definition. Instead, ordinary case variations produce broken navigation.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0095",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "CRLF becomes two spaces inside code spans. [parse.rs:1340](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/parse.rs:1340) processes CR and LF separately. CommonMark defines CRLF as one line ending, replaced by one space in code spans. Parsing `` `a\\r\\nb` `` produces `<code>a  b</code>` instead of `<code>a b</code>`. This changes literal code content in Windows-formatted Markdown.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0096",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Several block parsers do not recognize CR-only line endings. [scanners.rs:508](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/scanners.rs:508) searches only for LF. CommonMark also recognizes standalone CR. For example, `\"```rust\\rx\\r```\"` becomes a paragraph followed by an empty code block instead of a Rust code block containing `x`. Indented blocks also retain subsequent indentation incorrectly. Equivalent supported line endings should preserve document structure.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0097",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "The `getopts` feature can select a binary that cannot compile. [main.rs:25](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/main.rs:25) imports `html` unconditionally, while [Cargo.toml:27](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/Cargo.toml:27) requires only `getopts` for the binary. `cargo check --locked -p pulldown-cmark --no-default-features --features getopts` fails with E0432 because `html` is disabled. The same configuration with `--lib` passes, isolating the failure to binary feature configuration.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0098",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Link-label length counting rejects valid Unicode labels and accepts oversized ASCII labels. [linklabel.rs:122](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/linklabel.rs:122) increments the character count for each non-ASCII byte and skips ordinary ASCII characters. CommonMark permits at most 999 Unicode code points. A reference label containing 500 `\u00e9` characters fails to resolve, while one containing 1,000 ASCII `a` characters resolves. Controls with 499 `\u00e9` and 999 ASCII characters pass.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0099",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Wikilink source ranges omit the final bracket. [parse.rs:944](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/parse.rs:944) sets the end offset one byte too early. For `[[page]]`, the link\u2019s range selects `[[page]`. `into_offset_iter()` promises the corresponding Markdown source range; editors and source transformations using this range leave a closing bracket behind.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0100",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Repeated footnote references consume new display numbers. pulldown-cmark/src/html.rs:139. The FootnoteReference rendering arm calculates the next number on every occurrence and assigns it even when the label has already been seen. With ENABLE_FOOTNOTES, first[^a] second[^a] third[^b] and definitions for a and b therefore display reference numbers 1, 2, 3 rather than 1, 1, 2. Repeating a reference changes the displayed identity of the same footnote and shifts numbering for later notes.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0101",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "ATX heading closers mishandle tabs. [firstpass.rs:1655](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/firstpass.rs:1655) and [firstpass.rs:1664](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/firstpass.rs:1664) trim/check spaces without tabs. CommonMark permits tabs around closing hashes. `\"# foo\\t###\\t\\n\"` renders `<h1>foo\\t###\\t</h1>` instead of `<h1>foo</h1>`, exposing syntax characters as heading content.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0102",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Inline links accept a title without the required separator. [parse.rs:1156](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/parse.rs:1156) attempts title parsing even when no whitespace follows a nonempty destination. CommonMark requires separation between destination and title. `[a](<url>\"title\")` incorrectly emits a link with destination `url` and title `title`; it should not emit a link. The whitespace-separated control behaves correctly.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0103",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Subscript parsing can disable unrelated superscript parsing. [parse.rs:1596](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/parse.rs:1596) and [parse.rs:1614](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/parse.rs:1614) share a delimiter-search lower bound between carets and tildes. With superscript alone, `^a b~ c^` produces `<sup>a b~ c</sup>`. Enabling subscript as well makes the entire expression literal. An unmatched tilde should not invalidate the independent caret pair; combining documented extensions changes otherwise valid formatting.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0104",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Single-character heading attributes disappear. [firstpass.rs:2548](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/firstpass.rs:2548) skips every attribute token of length one. The public heading-attribute contract permits custom attributes without values. With `ENABLE_HEADING_ATTRIBUTES`, `# hi {x}` should retain `(\"x\", None)`, but emits an empty attribute list. Callers silently lose requested metadata.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0105",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "The added reproductions are retained in [review_regressions.rs](/work/tmp/review-crate/pulldown-cmark/tests/review_regressions.rs), [review_spec_variants.rs](/work/tmp/review-crate/pulldown-cmark/tests/review_spec_variants.rs), and [review_cli.py](/work/tmp/review_cli.py). Assertion failures indicate incorrect results; they are not parser panics.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0106",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Checks ran with `RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0`, Rust/Cargo **1.99.1**, on **aarch64 Linux**. Repository commands ran from `/work/crate`; added Rust tests ran from `/work/tmp/review-crate`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0107",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "| Command | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo test --locked -p pulldown-cmark` | Passed: 1,250 unit/integration tests and 5 doctests. |\n| `cargo test --locked -p pulldown-cmark --all-features` | Passed: 1,255 unit/integration tests and 5 doctests. |\n| `cargo test --locked -p pulldown-cmark --no-default-features` | Passed: 77 unit/integration tests and 2 doctests. |\n| `cargo build --locked -p pulldown-cmark` | Passed. |\n| `cargo check --locked -p pulldown-cmark --no-default-features --features getopts` | Failed: E0432, finding 8. Adding `--lib` passed. |\n| `cargo fmt --all --check` | Passed. |\n| `RUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' cargo doc --locked -p pulldown-cmark --all-features --no-deps` | Passed. |\n| `RUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' cargo doc --locked -p pulldown-cmark --no-default-features --no-deps` | Passed. |\n| `cargo clippy --locked -p pulldown-cmark --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings` | Pre-existing failure: four build-script lint errors at `build.rs:54`, `:63`, and `:117`. |\n| Same Clippy command without `-- -D warnings` | Completed successfully, with additional source/example/test warnings. |\n| `cargo test --locked -p pulldown-cmark --test review_regressions -- --test-threads=1` | 2 passed, 13 failed, covering 11 behavioral findings. |\n| `cargo test --locked -p pulldown-cmark --test review_spec_variants -- --nocapture` | Failed: all 652 default-option LF fixtures matched; normalized comparisons found 6 CRLF and 85 CR mismatches. |\n| `python3 /work/tmp/review_cli.py` | Three assertions failed, reproducing findings 3 and 4. |\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0108",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "No production Rust sources were edited. Added review tests and harness edits were confined to scratch space. Running `--all-features` enabled `gen-tests`, whose existing build script regenerated `tests/suite/*.rs` in the original checkout.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0109",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Coverage was package-focused and used ordinary local regression tests. MSRV 1.71.1, other architectures, x86 SIMD execution, release tests, and Miri were not run. No dedicated security assessment was performed. Last clock reading: **7.1274 of 45 minutes used**."
  },
  {
    "id": "P0110",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Found **19 behavior/build issues**. The existing package tests pass; targeted local regressions expose the following gaps. All behavior findings below were executed against the unchanged release source.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0111",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "CLI processing repeats earlier files \u2014 [main.rs:173](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/main.rs:173). `read_to_string` appends to the same buffer for every filename. Files containing `one\\n` and `two\\n` produce `<p>one</p>\\n<p>one\\ntwo</p>\\n`, duplicating the first document. Each file should be rendered once.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0112",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "CLI I/O failures return success \u2014 [main.rs:184](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/main.rs:184), [main.rs:219](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/main.rs:219). Invalid UTF-8 on stdin produces empty output, no diagnostic and exit status 0. Writing to a closed output pipe also exits 0. Read/write failures should propagate so callers can detect lost input or output; buffered output also needs an explicit checked flush.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0113",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Linking a wiki image corrupts its destination \u2014 [parse.rs:642](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/parse.rs:642). With `ENABLE_WIKILINKS`, `[![[foo.png]]](bar)` should produce an image linking to `bar`. Instead it produces `<p>[<img src=\"bar\" alt=\"](bar)\" /></p>`. The successful wikilink path leaves regular bracket-stack entries available for subsequent parsing, allowing the image node to be overwritten.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0114",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Uppercase HTML closing tags fail to end blocks \u2014 [firstpass.rs:1250](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/firstpass.rs:1250). CommonMark requires case-insensitive matching here, but termination uses case-sensitive `contains`. For `<pre>\\nx\\n</PRE>\\n*after*\\n`, `*after*` remains raw HTML-block content instead of becoming an emphasized paragraph. Subsequent document content can be misparsed.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0115",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Tabs prevent code fences from closing \u2014 [scanners.rs:528](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/scanners.rs:528). CommonMark permits spaces or tabs after a closing fence; this scanner accepts only spaces. For `\"```\\nx\\n```\\t\\nafter\\n\"`, the closing fence and `after` remain inside the code block instead of ending it and starting a paragraph.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0116",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Case-insensitive footnote matching produces broken links and numbering \u2014 [html.rs:138](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/html.rs:138). The parser accepts `[^A]` and `[^a]` against definition `[^a]: definition` through case-folded lookup. The renderer nevertheless emits targets `#A` and `#a`, numbers them 1 and 2, and labels the sole definition 2. Both references should share a number and resolve to the same definition.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0117",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "The `getopts` feature can select an unbuildable binary \u2014 [main.rs:25](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/main.rs:25). The binary requires `getopts` in the manifest but unconditionally imports feature-gated `html`. `cargo check --locked -p pulldown-cmark --no-default-features --features getopts` fails with E0432. The binary\u2019s feature requirements should include its HTML dependency.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0118",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "An unmatched caret cancels valid strikethrough \u2014 [parse.rs:1614](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/parse.rs:1614). Carets and tildes share a delimiter-search lower bound. With superscript and strikethrough enabled, `~~a b^ c~~` renders literally; it should render `<del>a b^ c</del>`. Attempting to close unmatched superscript incorrectly excludes an existing tilde opener.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0119",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Broken-link callback overrides references that already have definitions. pulldown-cmark/src/parse.rs:343. Parser::new_with_broken_link_callback invokes the supplied resolver even after finding an in-document reference definition. A callback that always supplies /fallback therefore replaces the destination and title of [ok][known] despite [known]: /defined \"Defined\" being present. Applications using a callback to fill missing links also rewrite links explicitly authored in the document.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0120",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Subscript alone suppresses unrelated inline parsing \u2014 [parse.rs:993](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/parse.rs:993). With only `ENABLE_SUBSCRIPT`, `~~*a*~~`, `~~[a](b)~~` and ``~~`a`~~`` all render literally. Unsupported double-tilde delimiters should remain text while their contents retain ordinary emphasis, link and code parsing. Creating a text node with children causes those children to be skipped.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0121",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "CRLF becomes two spaces inside code spans \u2014 [parse.rs:1340](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/parse.rs:1340). CommonMark treats CRLF as one line ending. `` `a\\r\\nb` `` yields code text `a  b`, whereas LF and CR versions yield `a b`. Each byte is replaced separately, changing code content in ordinary Windows-format documents.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0122",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "CR-only line endings break block parsing \u2014 [scanners.rs:508](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/scanners.rs:508). `scan_nextline` searches only for LF, although CommonMark also recognizes standalone CR. For example, `\"    x\\r\\rafter\\r\"` becomes one code block containing `after`, rather than a code block followed by a paragraph. Fenced-code and HTML-block probes also fail; LF and CRLF controls pass.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0123",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Wikilink source ranges omit the final bracket \u2014 [parse.rs:944](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/parse.rs:944). `[[page]]` has eight bytes, but its start/end link events report `0..7`. Piped links and wiki images have the same error. The documented corresponding-source-range contract requires the complete construct; source-based editing can otherwise leave a stray bracket.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0124",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Reference-label length counts bytes incorrectly \u2014 [linklabel.rs:122](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/linklabel.rs:122). CommonMark permits at most 999 characters. Ordinary ASCII characters are not counted, while every non-ASCII UTF-8 byte is counted. A 1,000-character ASCII label is accepted; valid labels containing 500 `\u00e9` characters or 334 `\u754c` characters are rejected, leaving links and definitions as literal text.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0125",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Tabs are not trimmed around ATX closing markers \u2014 [firstpass.rs:1655](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/firstpass.rs:1655). CommonMark permits tabs around closing hashes and strips trailing tabs. Both `# heading\\t###` and `# heading ###\\t` retain literal hashes in the heading. The trimming logic recognizes spaces only.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0126",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Nested inline end tags prematurely terminate image alt-text collection. pulldown-cmark/src/html.rs:484. HtmlWriter::raw_text stops collecting an outer image description when it reaches the end of nested emphasis or a nested image. For ![before *em* ![inner](inner.png) after](outer.png) tail, this closes the outer alt attribute too early and renders the remaining description as ordinary page text. Image descriptions containing nested inline markup consequently lose their trailing alt text.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0127",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Tabs incorrectly create hard line breaks \u2014 [firstpass.rs:849](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/firstpass.rs:849). Hard breaks require two spaces or a backslash, but the implementation counts all non-newline ASCII whitespace. `foo\\t\\t\\nbar`, `foo \\t\\nbar` and `foo\\t \\nbar` each produce `<br />` instead of a soft break, changing document layout.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0128",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Valid HTML with tab-separated unquoted attributes is escaped \u2014 [scanners.rs:452](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/scanners.rs:452). Tabs must terminate an unquoted attribute value. For `a <b x=one\\ty=two>z</b>`, the opening tag becomes `&lt;b x=one\\ty=two&gt;` while the closing tag remains HTML. Valid embedded markup is rendered as text because the value scanner consumes the tab.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0129",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Invalid table alignment syntax becomes a table \u2014 [scanners.rs:675](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/scanners.rs:675). The bundled GFM contract permits colons only at delimiter-cell edges. A delimiter cell `-:-` is nevertheless accepted as right-aligned. Ordinary prose or an incomplete table containing that sequence is converted into a table instead of remaining text.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0130",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Single-character valueless heading attributes disappear \u2014 [firstpass.rs:2548](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/firstpass.rs:2548). With heading attributes enabled, `# heading {a bb c=d}` emits `bb=\"\" c=\"d\"` but drops `a`. The documented custom-attribute syntax does not impose a two-character minimum. Callers silently lose an explicitly supplied attribute.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0131",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Tabbed fence metadata leaks into the language class \u2014 [html.rs:261](/work/crate/pulldown-cmark/src/html.rs:261). The renderer\u2019s first-word language convention splits only on spaces. A fence with info `rust\\tmore` produces `class=\"language-rust\\tmore\"` instead of `class=\"language-rust\"`, turning following metadata into an additional HTML class. This is a smaller renderer-consistency issue.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0132",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "The behavior expectations above come from the public API documentation, bundled CommonMark/GFM specifications, extension specifications and source inspection. The added assertions are in [regressions.rs](/work/tmp/review/tests/regressions.rs); CLI assertions are in [cli_checks.py](/work/tmp/review/cli_checks.py). Existing tests miss these cases; notably, the generated-suite helper enables many runtime options together, which does not exercise subscript in isolation.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0133",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Executed checks used Rust/Cargo **1.99.1**, aarch64 Linux, with `RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0`. Commands below ran from `/work/crate` unless stated otherwise.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0134",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "| Command | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo test --locked -p pulldown-cmark` | Passed: 1,255 tests, including doctests |\n| `cargo test --locked -p pulldown-cmark --all-features` | Passed: 1,260 tests |\n| `cargo test --locked -p pulldown-cmark --no-default-features` | Passed: 79 tests; HTML suites disabled |\n| `cargo check --locked -p pulldown-cmark --no-default-features --features getopts` | Failed: E0432, finding 7 |\n| `cargo fmt --all --check` | Passed |\n| `RUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' cargo doc --locked -p pulldown-cmark --all-features --no-deps` | Passed |\n| `RUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' cargo doc --locked -p pulldown-cmark --no-default-features --no-deps` | Passed |\n| `cargo clippy --locked -p pulldown-cmark --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings` | Failed before source linting: four pre-existing build-script diagnostics |\n| `cargo clippy --locked -p pulldown-cmark --all-targets --features serde,simd -- -D warnings` | Failed: 23 pre-existing library diagnostics, including attribute spacing, documentation indentation and style lints |\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0135",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "From `/work/tmp/review`, `cargo test --locked --offline --test regressions -- --nocapture --test-threads=1` finished with **16 failed regression assertions and two passing controls**. `python3 /work/tmp/review/cli_checks.py` produced three failed assertions. These are expected-versus-actual failures in added tests, not evidence of parser panics. Logs are in [final-regressions.log](/work/tmp/final-regressions.log) and [cli.log](/work/tmp/cli.log).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0136",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "No production source was edited. Scratch files were added under `/work/tmp`; the all-features run enabled `gen-tests`, which rewrote the existing generated `tests/suite` files.\n\n"
